      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Instruct Python to read the cvs and parse the data type of the column named Date as a datetime object instead of text. Also we create a new column where we calculate the distance between the lowest price of the day and the lower band."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "EEV8Zknxa4Wj"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "url = (\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/fkottas/Teaching-Courses/refs/heads/main/Machine%20Learning%20in%20Finance/2026-2027/lectures/lecture-00-01/data/finance-charts-apple.csv\")\n",
        "prices = pd.read_csv(url, parse_dates = [\"Date\"])\n",
        "\n",
        "prices[\"low_vs_dn\"] = prices[\"AAPL.Low\"] - prices[\"dn\"]"
