    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The data show that Apple's daily lowest price generally remains above the technical lower band, as evidenced by the positive mean distances across all three observed years. The distribution chart confirms this, displaying a right-skewed pattern where breaches below the band are infrequent. However, the time chart reveals that when these negative breaches do occur, they are not randomly scattered; rather, they cluster during specific periods of extreme downward volatility, most notably in mid-2015. Additionally, the annual summary indicates that the average distance from the lower band increased progressively from 2015 to 2017, suggesting a reduction in extreme downward price pressure over this specific timeframe."
      ],
